  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1243 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nThe center of the upper ridge will move off to the east and this \nwill allow for broad upper level troughing to take over just to our \nwest. Several fronts look to come into or close to the region along \nwith potential for better rain chances through the week. At this \ntime, Tuesday looks like the best day in terms of chances for precip \nbut each day next week shows potential, the most potential we have \nseen in quite some time. The other benefit to this increased chances \nfor rain is it should keep our temperatures lower and closer to \naverage or even below for this time of year.",
